sequence-diagram

typeface clean
styleMode plain
colorMode bold
autoNumber on

User [color: blue]
Frontend [color: purple]
Router [label: "Express Router", color: green]
Limiter [label: "Signup Rate Limiter", color: red]
LimitStore [label: "In-memory Rate Store", color: gray]
JsonParser [label: "express.json()", color: yellow]
Validator [label: "Zod Validator", color: red]
Controller [label: "Auth Controller", color: green]
Service [label: "Auth Service", color: orange]
Repository [label: "User Repository", color: cyan]
Database [label: PostgreSQL, color: blue]
EmailProvider [label: Gmail, color: purple]
ErrorHandler [label: "Express Default Error Handler", color: gray]

User > Frontend: Enter email, username, and password
Frontend > Router: POST /api/auth/signup

Router > Limiter: Run signupRateLimiter using request IP
Limiter > LimitStore: Read and increment attempt count
LimitStore > Limiter: Return current attempt count

break [label: More than 5 attempts in 15 minutes, color: red] {
  Limiter > Frontend: 429 Too Many Requests with RateLimit headers
  Frontend > User: Ask user to wait before trying again
}

Limiter > Router: next()
Router > JsonParser: Parse JSON request body

break [label: Malformed JSON, color: red] {
  JsonParser > ErrorHandler: next(SyntaxError)
  ErrorHandler > Frontend: 400 Bad Request
  Frontend > User: Display request error
}

JsonParser > Router: Parsed request body
Router > Validator: Validate body with signupSchema

break [label: Validation fails, color: red] {
  Validator > Frontend: 400 JSON with flattened Zod errors
  Frontend > User: Display field validation errors
}

Validator > Router: Attach data to req.validatedBody and call next()
Router > Controller: signupController(req, res, next)
Controller > Service: signup(req.validatedBody)

Service > Service: Lowercase and trim email and username
Service > Service: Hash password with bcrypt (12 rounds)
Service > Service: Generate 32-byte raw verification token
Service > Service: SHA-256 hash token and set 24-hour expiry

Service > Repository: createUser(normalized data, password hash, token hash, expiry)
Repository > Database: INSERT user (emailVerified defaults to false)

break [label: Email or username already exists (Prisma P2002), color: red] {
  Database > Repository: Unique-constraint error
  Repository > Service: Throw Error with statusCode 409
  Service > Controller: Reject signup promise
  Controller > ErrorHandler: next(error)
  ErrorHandler > Frontend: 409 Conflict
  Frontend > User: Display duplicate-account message
}

break [label: Unexpected database error, color: red] {
  Database > Repository: Database error
  Repository > Service: Re-throw error
  Service > Controller: Reject signup promise
  Controller > ErrorHandler: next(error)
  ErrorHandler > Frontend: 500 Internal Server Error
  Frontend > User: Display generic error
}

Database > Repository: Return created user fields
Repository > Service: Created user

Service > EmailProvider: Send verification link containing raw token

alt [label: Email sent, color: green] {
  EmailProvider > Service: Return message info
  Service > Service: Log email message ID
}
else [label: Email delivery fails, color: orange] {
  EmailProvider > Service: Throw delivery error
  Service > Service: Log error and keep the account
}

Service > Controller: Return check-your-email message
Controller > Frontend: 201 Created JSON
Frontend > User: Ask user to verify their email

legend [position: bottom-left] {
  [color: green, label: Success path]
  [color: red, label: Request-stopping error]
  [color: orange, label: Non-fatal email error]
}
